<Base title="Editorial policy"><div class="wrap"><article class="prose"><div class="eyebrow">Our standards</div><h1>Evidence before speed.</h1><p>We aim to link to original sources, distinguish reported claims from independently established facts, and explain uncertainty. Different websites are not necessarily independent if they rely on the same reporting.</p><h2>AI-assisted work</h2><p>We may use locally hosted AI to help research or prepare drafts. AI can make mistakes, invent details or misread sources. A human editor is responsible for reviewing and approving every article before publication. Sources are linked so readers can inspect them.</p><h2>Corrections</h2><p>When we discover a material mistake, we review the evidence and update the article with an explanation. See our <a href="/corrections/">corrections policy</a>.</p><h2>Independence</h2><p>We aim to distinguish news from opinion or analysis, identify promotional material, and disclose relevant relationships when applicable.</p></article></div></Base>
